  "goodToKnow": "Der Boykott is a boycott: zum Boykott aufrufen, einen Boykott verhängen. Boykottieren means to boycott. On 1 April 1933, the Nazis organised a nationwide Boykott of Jewish shops, doctors and lawyers, an early step in persecution. West Germany joined the US-led boycott of the 1980 Moscow Olympics. The word comes from Charles Boycott, an Irish land agent ostracised in 1880. Plural: die Boykotte."
